{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20","id":1455193,"title":"Some simple ideas for Appearance houserules to make it useful? Revised/3e/V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-19T07:34:31-07:00","id":1455193,"title":"Some simple ideas for Appearance houserules to make it useful? Revised/3e/V20","content":"We all know that looks can get you far in life even without education or high IQ (can get you even to hollywood even if you don't have talent). But by default Apperance in Vampire TM is useless and that's bad becasue many players love to play that pale, sexy vampires but that costs dots that do nothing. So I would like to hear your houserules for it. Simple ones that are easy to remember and use.<br /> <br /> I think of the following (forgive my English, I am not native speaker):<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Appearance is not just a physical attribute and how good your face look. It's also how you present yourself on social events, parties, official meeting etc. You know the latest fashion trends and what suit to chose for meeting with Price and what for business meeting. You have different pair of shoes for every occasion and you know where you can allow yourself to wear tie and tied your hair and when you can allow yourself to wear mini-skirt and aggresive makeup. You also feel in formal cloths like in your own skin and you are not even slightly uncomfortable in evening dress on high heels.<br /> <br /> System: In every social situation where good look and presentation would give you advantage you can add your Apperance atribute value to your social dice pool of Charisma and Manipulation rolls (how many is up to Storyteller but minimum 1 extra dice). This does not work with powers that force your target to feel certain emotions or obey you, like Domination or some Presence powers like: Dreadful Gaze or Summon (but may work with Awe or Entrancement)&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> So for example if you want to talk your way as a male vampire through some male bodyguards that are straight you won't get Apperance bonus, becasue they don't care. They might even be slightly irritated by how good you look.<br /> <br /> But if you were a female vampire or met a homosexual bodyguard - suddenly your social dicepool for your Charisma + Emapthy rolls will increase becasue you are just so good looking that even a slight hope of chance to hit on you will carry you through a lot of dialogues. With Appearance 5 your Storyteller gives you 4 extra dice to add.<br /> <br /> But when you meet atractive female that is married that bonus may be reduced to 2 bonus dice. Yes, you are so handsome that she will flirt with you but she is devoted to her husband so she won't be as easy as that collage girl from club yesterday night.<br /> <br /> Same if your party got invited to talk about business with Ventrue CEO. You know that this calls for single-breasted jacket in techno strethch from Prada and so the Ventrue CEO is impressed by your taste and professionalism. 3 Extra dice.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Little bit Storyteller depending but I feel this could at least make Appearance &quot;called for&quot; in every social situation, giving it an important role and not to be forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 07-19-2021, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T09:15:35-07:00","id":1455200,"title":"","content":"In my homebrew, I stole Heavy Arms' suggestions from another thread and combined it with Exalted 3e's rules. So it covers body language, poise, composure and unspoken communication as well as looks. <br /> <br /> You can add a bonus to positive social influence actions equal to the difference between your Appearance and your opponent's Wits, if appropriate, which makes it very useful. You roll it with Subterfuge to hide your intentions from casual observers (e.g., to blend into a crowd or hide your murderous intent at Elysium).<br /> <br /> Anyone can also take the 0-pt. Flaw Hideous to make your Appearance a marker of how horrific you are. It applies your Appearance as a penalty to seduction attempts (unless your target is into that), but adds to Intimidation attempts or similar in the same way standard Appearance adds to 'positive' social influence actions.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Nosferatu always have to take the Hideous Flaw, and they tend to have high Appearance rather than low, but it means something very different to a Toreador's high Appearance. I like that change to the rules, since Appearance is no longer a dump stat and Nosferatu ugliness is a weapon as much as a Flaw.<br /> <br /> So far it works great, and is better than the Composure stat of V5 and VTR because it's not as narrow; it feels more vampiric to have an Attribute specifically for seduction, intimidation and posing; and you can use it for performing or ritualistic behaviours too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T10:09:45-07:00","id":1455204,"title":"","content":"I think appearance gets a bad wrap, honestly, but that's because how it is mechanically in default rules.<br /> <br /> I give everyone a speciality at appearance 1, and appearance specialities are very important because they dictate the specifics of how people respond to your good/bad looks. Appearance specialities can also change. The main thing here, is that there are high-risk/high-high reward specialities where some people may react exceptionally possitively but other people will be offput by your speciality, and more neutral, inoffensive specialities. Appearance specialities are relatively dynamic, and you can change them with effort.<br /> I basically make everyone judgmental. If you've got 1 appearance, people don't want to talk to you. If you've got 2 appearance, people don't have incentive to talk to you, but aren't particularly adverse. Perhaps if they're a little desperate at the club you'll get some attention. Three appearance is useful. 4 appearance veers into a realm where your good looks have a few drawbacks, as people are threatened by your good looks (the severity of course influenced by your speciality) but more often they will go out of their way to accommodate you. but at 5 you're an angel that makes 4 feel inferior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T12:05:26-07:00","id":1455208,"title":"","content":"While I hate the first impression rule (limiting Social die pools to Appearance when you first meet someone), I do often make people roll Appearance for any Social rolls they make with someone they don't know. Even for Disciplines. THIS has gotten some players to feel like Appearance matters when they go to Dominate some random mortal and I'm like &quot;now don't forget, it's Appearance + Leadership, not Manipulation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T14:30:14-07:00","id":1455214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20#post1455193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">System: In every social situation where good look and presentation would give you advantage you can add your Apperance atribute value to your social dice pool of Charisma and Manipulation rolls (how many is up to Storyteller but minimum 1 extra dice).</div> </div> </div> </div>This probably isn't a great solution. The system strains heavily once dice pools start going over 10. It's just not calibrated for characters that can get 15 dice for basic mundane actions as humans let alone supernaturals that can add even more on to that. A small bonus of 0 to 3 dice could work (ala the suggestion to use Exalted 3e's rule) because it's situational and doesn't run into:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So for example if you want to talk your way as a male vampire through some male bodyguards that are straight you won't get Apperance bonus, becasue they don't care. They might even be slightly irritated by how good you look. </div> </div> </div>This. These sorts of metrics are always a pain in play. One of the things I like to keep in mind when thinking about house rules is that a rule's job is to remove tension between the players and the GM by creating a neutral arbitrary baseline to refer to. When you put too much on GM fiat, esp. regarding cultural norms and customs with a lot of disagreements about how &quot;real&quot; or strong they are, you run the risk of subverting the very point of a rule by creating points where the players and GM are predictably going to argue (even though both are doing so for good reasons, not just one person being an ass).<br /> <br /> Why doesn't Appearance matter to straight men talking to other straight men? Just because it's not a matter of seduction doesn't mean looks don't stop mattering.<br /> <br /> A well dressed man in the latest style that carries himself surely and confidently is going to have a much easier time talking his way into a nightclub than a man that looks like he just crawled out of a dumpster and is stumbling around like he's already dangerously drunk. When you make the bonus dependent on this sort of rules call, you're both undermining the idea that Appearance isn't just good looks, and you're prompting the GM and players to get into game-distracting arguments over whether or not looks should matter in a given situation.<br /> <br /> This is why the aforementioned Exalted 3e rule is a bonus of Appearance vs. another trait. It completely avoids any such arguments because it isn't about whether or not looks should matter for the bonus to apply, but how well a target of social influence resists their natural urge to judge based on looks.<br /> <br /> Things like sexuality, dress codes, and so on can just be handled by difficulty modifiers to rolls instead of directly interfacing with Appearance's base rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455200#post1455200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my homebrew, I stole Heavy Arms' suggestions from another thread and combined it with Exalted 3e's rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Name check, woo! Also, the Ex3 add on is an interesting one, I might need to toy with that for myself at some point.<br /> <br /> To restate what's being referenced:<br /> <br /> In my WoD homebrew, I treat Appearance like any other Attribute. No &quot;first impression&quot; dice-cap non-sense. In order to make it valuable though, it's specifically the Attribute of non-verbal communication (which is really important because so much of normal human interaction relies on non-verbal cues even if the digital era is starting to pressure us to adapt to a reality where we lose a lot of those cues).<br /> <br /> One of my go to examples is dancing. Dexterity + Performance is great for perfectly executing difficult routines when you're looking at something like an audition or competition. Appearance + Performance is what makes your dancing stir emotions in people even if it's not 100% perfect to some predetermined set of moves. Dancers (from high brow ballet to dirty strip joints) might need some high baseline Dexterity to be good at their job, but Appearance is what separates the average and the top. The prima ballerina doesn't have to be the best technical dancer in the ballet, but they have to be the one that knows how each of those moves tells a story, and captures the audience so they feel the emotional weight of the story without a single word spoken. The best tipped stripper isn't the one that has the best conventional looks off stage, or again the best technical dancer, but rather the one that's best able to perform on a thin line between showing too little and showing too much so that the audience is hooked on wanting to keep watching to see more.<br /> <br /> Though as adambeyoncelowe noted, my homebrew makes sure to stress that all forms of non-verbal social interactions default to Appearance. Blending in with a crowd, threatening someone, being a good shoulder to cry on... all things that can be primarily accomplished by sending the right non-verbal signals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455208#post1455208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I hate the first impression rule (limiting Social die pools to Appearance when you first meet someone), I do often make people roll Appearance for any Social rolls they make with someone they don't know. Even for Disciplines. THIS has gotten some players to feel like Appearance matters when they go to Dominate some random mortal and I'm like &quot;now don't forget, it's Appearance + Leadership, not Manipulation&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't like that &quot;have to roll Appearance&quot; for first impressions thing. It completely destroys a lot of archetypal characters who's words make up for not being great as presentation. It's also very... unreal... to how we perceive things. Since social situations aren't handled with the level of detail as things like combat, your first impression isn't just the first 3 seconds of seeing them, but also the first things that you speak, and lots of other factors.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that in the desire to fix perceived problems with one Attribute, you don't want to cause more. I usually point to Exalted 2e here because it tried to make Appearance matter, but in many ways over corrected and Appearance became the social Attribute that really mattered and felt more like Dexterity than a balance Attribute. Letting Appearance be rolled for lots and lots of Discipline activation just encourages high Appearance characters that &quot;social-hobo&quot; around because as long as they don't engage with long term social conflicts, they get to have great rolls on all their stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T23:44:59-07:00","id":1455240,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Heavy. Appearance is basically my favourite social stat now. Although Charisma and Manipulation are essential for all forms of spoken communication, Appearance has some decent utility. And I really like Hideous from Exalted 3e, so that works too, since I want the Gangrel and Nosferatu to not ignore one of their nine Attributes outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T07:02:21-07:00","id":1455252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455200#post1455200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my homebrew, I stole Heavy Arms' suggestions from another thread and combined it with Exalted 3e's rules. So it covers body language, poise, composure and unspoken communication as well as looks.<br /> <br /> You can add a bonus to positive social influence actions equal to the difference between your Appearance and your opponent's Wits, if appropriate, which makes it very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like it but then if average NPC Wits is 2 and very high Appearance is 4, then it gives 2 more dice. While that does sound nice, the player could just on character creation put those 2 dice from Appearance into Charisma and 1 in Manipulation and have premanent increase without relying on Appearance being or not relevant is said situation. I kind of wish to make it (like Charisma and Manipulation) useful all the time in specific scenarios, same as Charisma and Manipulation is. You want to send someone to smooth talk a guard and take her time and keep her busy- you send high Charisma guy. You want to make sure we negotiate the best deal possible with arm dealers - you send high Manipulation guy. You want to seduce a daughter of company owner so we can kidnap her outside of this hotel - you should said highest Appearance guy (probably with Charisma as second) etc. I want it being rolled and be relevant.<br /> <br /> I like the body language idea of yours Adam - so maybe I will do it like this:<br /> <br /> In non-spoken communication social interaction (dancing for seduction in loud club, inviting someone to follow you with your eyes and body language, making woman not screem when you run away and bump on her in alley etc.) you would roll Appearance + *Social Skill*.<br /> <br /> I like First Impression to matter since that's realistic but I would change that to just Appearance + *Social Skill* roll. Note that not every time you need a First Impression (same like not every time you need Manipulation if you can work with your Charisma and counterwise). But for example an untrusty Ventrue or a anti-social Brujah in the corner of Elysium definitely doesn't look like they will just let you sit next to them and start working with your Charisma/Manipulation. You need to make good First Impression. On the other hand many people are more open and you don't need that, so it depends. But for example when you pretend something in non-verbal way you roll Appearance + Performance to convience someone.<br /> <br /> I want Appearance to matter in same way as Charisma and Manipulation simply becasue social characters in pre-V5 tend to just pack into Charisma and Manipulation, ignoring Appearance and that had little consequences becasue everybody were ignoring RAW &quot;First Impression&quot; rules (correctly becasue they are dumb) in false argument of &quot;you can be ugly but it doesn't matter if you are well-spoken&quot;. Which is not true as hitting on grils has shown through centuries. You won't have chance for talk if they walk away from you cause you look like potato. I want all 3 to have equally important impact so you have to chose. Same like with STR, DEX and Stamina. You can't pack all of them, you have to choose if you want to have them all on semi-good level or maybe one on really high and rest on low and so on. I would for example see Assassin wanting to have high Appearance becasue you need to use your body-language + clothing choice to not seem like a threat, to make people treat you as harmless or nice person etc. without talking and speaking becasue that's not what you want to do.<br /> <br /> Appearance matters a lot in real life. For example I am very Charismatic person in real-life but not Appearance 4-5 definitely. However I have friend who is not really charismatic or eloquent but he is model (Appearance 4-5 in my opinion) and he achieves same effect when we are at party as me (making contacts etc.) but I have to work harder on that while he is just... well handsome and stylish. All Social stats matter in life. But no imagine a guys who is both Appearance 4-5 and Charisma 4-5. Jeez, that's an anime villan for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 07-20-2021, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T07:10:50-07:00","id":1455253,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, this statement right there &quot;Letting Appearance be rolled for lots and lots of Discipline activation just encourages high Appearance characters that &quot;social-hobo&quot; around because as long as they don't engage with long term social conflicts, they get to have great rolls on all their stuff.&quot;, has me a little confused. Wouldn't playing characters like this be a disadvantage in of itself? You'd never be able to truly ingratiate yourself with Kindred society, you'd have a hard time developing a network of mortal pawns, and even the Blood Bond only lowers Social roll difficulties by 1 (and Mesmerize still needs 3 successes to get anyone to do something they find out of the ordinary). So yeah, for the one scene you meet someone for the first time, great, you can have a great Social die pool. Then...what, you run away and never encounter those people again because they might find out you only have Charisma 2? I don't mind if you don't like my solution, any reason you have is valid- but that objection does seem a bit absurd. This doesn't invalidate non-pretty but charismatic or manipulative people at all, it just means they don't have the immediate advantage of a beautiful person, an advantage which is short lived at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T07:41:31-07:00","id":1455258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455253#post1455253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it just means they don't have the immediate advantage of a beautiful person, an advantage which is short lived at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I don't know about that. I would like a Appearance 5 woman/man to meet regulary with me, even if her/his Charisma is not that great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Wouldn't you like young Jessica Alba to be your friend and meet with you regulary even though she doesn't have high Charisma and is non-Manipulative at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or do you think Brad Pitt/George Clouney Appearance 4 would be &quot;short lived&quot; advantage at best becasue he doesn't have high Charisma? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Life doesn't work that way. Looks is really really important in our society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T10:41:54-07:00","id":1455264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455252#post1455252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of like it but then if average NPC Wits is 2 and very high Appearance is 4, then it gives 2 more dice. While that does sound nice, the player could just on character creation put those 2 dice from Appearance into Charisma and 1 in Manipulation and have premanent increase without relying on Appearance being or not relevant is said situation. I kind of wish to make it (like Charisma and Manipulation) useful all the time in specific scenarios, same as Charisma and Manipulation is. You want to send someone to smooth talk a guard and take her time and keep her busy- you send high Charisma guy. You want to make sure we negotiate the best deal possible with arm dealers - you send high Manipulation guy. You want to seduce a daughter of company owner so we can kidnap her outside of this hotel - you should said highest Appearance guy (probably with Charisma as second) etc. I want it being rolled and be relevant.<br /> <br /> I like the body language idea of yours Adam - so maybe I will do it like this:<br /> <br /> In non-spoken communication social interaction (dancing for seduction in loud club, inviting someone to follow you with your eyes and body language, making woman not screem when you run away and bump on her in alley etc.) you would roll Appearance + *Social Skill*.<br /> <br /> I like First Impression to matter since that's realistic but I would change that to just Appearance + *Social Skill* roll. Note that not every time you need a First Impression (same like not every time you need Manipulation if you can work with your Charisma and counterwise). But for example an untrusty Ventrue or a anti-social Brujah in the corner of Elysium definitely doesn't look like they will just let you sit next to them and start working with your Charisma/Manipulation. You need to make good First Impression. On the other hand many people are more open and you don't need that, so it depends. But for example when you pretend something in non-verbal way you roll Appearance + Performance to convience someone.<br /> <br /> I want Appearance to matter in same way as Charisma and Manipulation simply becasue social characters in pre-V5 tend to just pack into Charisma and Manipulation, ignoring Appearance and that had little consequences becasue everybody were ignoring RAW &quot;First Impression&quot; rules (correctly becasue they are dumb) in false argument of &quot;you can be ugly but it doesn't matter if you are well-spoken&quot;. Which is not true as hitting on grils has shown through centuries. You won't have chance for talk if they walk away from you cause you look like potato. I want all 3 to have equally important impact so you have to chose. Same like with STR, DEX and Stamina. You can't pack all of them, you have to choose if you want to have them all on semi-good level or maybe one on really high and rest on low and so on. I would for example see Assassin wanting to have high Appearance becasue you need to use your body-language + clothing choice to not seem like a threat, to make people treat you as harmless or nice person etc. without talking and speaking becasue that's not what you want to do.<br /> <br /> Appearance matters a lot in real life. For example I am very Charismatic person in real-life but not Appearance 4-5 definitely. However I have friend who is not really charismatic or eloquent but he is model (Appearance 4-5 in my opinion) and he achieves same effect when we are at party as me (making contacts etc.) but I have to work harder on that while he is just... well handsome and stylish. All Social stats matter in life. But no imagine a guys who is both Appearance 4-5 and Charisma 4-5. Jeez, that's an anime villan for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I wasn't clear, but that bonus is *in addition* to using Appearance as a rolled Attribute.<br /> <br /> So you can use Appearance + Subterfuge to seduce someone non-verbally. You can use Appearance + Performance to move someone with your dancing. You can use Appearance + Stealth to blend into a crowd. You can use Appearance + Etiquette to complete an intricate social ceremony.<br /> <br /> But if you're rolling Charisma + Subterfuge, you can *also* take a bonus of (your Appearance - their Wits). <br /> <br /> So Appearance is really quite powerful in my system, because it can be rolled in a dice pool or provide a partial bonus to another dice pool where it's relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-21-2021, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T12:08:13-07:00","id":1455272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455258#post1455258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, I don't know about that. I would like a Appearance 5 woman/man to meet regulary with me, even if her/his Charisma is not that great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Wouldn't you like young Jessica Alba to be your friend and meet with you regulary even though she doesn't have high Charisma and is non-Manipulative at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or do you think Brad Pitt/George Clouney Appearance 4 would be &quot;short lived&quot; advantage at best becasue he doesn't have high Charisma? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Life doesn't work that way. Looks is really really important in our society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man trust me, it don't matter how hot she is, if she's a crazy witch with no people skills, ABORT ABORT!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T12:29:14-07:00","id":1455275,"title":"","content":"This discussion is pretty awesome and I love most of the ideas here.<br /> <br /> Using Appearance as a modifier on appropriate &quot;positive&quot; social rolls (seduction, and some subterfuge/leadership rolls) - I will be doing this going forward with a modifier of -1 to +3 (App 1 is -1 die on social rolls, 2 is zero, 3 is +1, 4 is +2, 5 is +3). I also never thought of using Appearance for Nosferatu and I think this is a fanastic Idea, giving a 0 to +4 die bonus on Intimidation and thereby removing it as a &quot;dump stat&quot;, and forever meaning that no Nosferatu can use a discipline with a dice pool that relies on appearance. This kind of makes Nosferatu less goofy and more frightening, IMO.<br /> <br /> And using Appearance for non-verbal social rolls is also a winner. Thanks Heavy Arms.<br /> <br /> Thanks all for the ideas!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T13:47:50-07:00","id":1455278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455272#post1455272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Man trust me, it don't matter how hot she is, if she's a crazy witch with no people skills, ABORT ABORT!</div> </div> </div> </div>But who said you want to do long-relationship with them. It's just nice to meet with them becasue they look good. Nobody says anything about serious relationship.<br /> <br /> Besides Appearance 5 and Charisma 1 doesn't mean person is mean or bad. Just that she is not charismatic, but looks nice. She might be nice.<br /> <br /> I would take Appearance 4 and Charisma 1 but nice girl over Appearance 5 + Charisma 5 mean one any day.<br /> <br /> What I want to say is that looks matter and it's nothing negative. Everyone prefer good-looking people, that's how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T23:35:30-07:00","id":1455294,"title":"","content":"For reference, here are my house rules:<br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> Appearance is a measure of body language, subtle expression, composure and physical presence. It is the Attribute most closely tied to one's Demeanor and Bearing, and hence is useful for disguising one's true intent or passing furtive messages without uttering a word. Appearance covers non-verbal communication, including appearing nondescript, blending in, or passing oneself off as someone of another class, rank or profession.<br /> <br /> The most obvious examples of Appearance come from entertainment: a dancer might use Appearance to convey joy through his movements; an actor might use Appearance to embody her grief or inner conflict when playing a silent contract killer. But there are plenty of examples, too, in everyday life: a bouncer might use Appearance to exude a sense of threat; a police officer might use it to appear more authoritative; a politician might use it to portray sincerity or authenticity. <br /> <br /> A vampire might find several of these uses pertinent. She might give off an aura of vulnerability to attract her prey. She might wish to present herself as trustworthy at Elysium, even as she plans to undermine the Prince. She might even use it to communicate silently with her pack mates when imprisoned behind enemy lines.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Poor: You're an open book. You're clumsy, obvious and ungraceful.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Average: You can act sad at a funeral but you're not winning any Oscars.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Good: You were good in drama class. You're good at giving off the right cues to get what you want.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Exceptional: You're Al Pacino in The Godfather. You're Amy Winehouse before she even opens her mouth.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Outstanding: With but a look or a slight shift of your weight, hardened criminals break down weeping or rush to help you. By shifting your features, you become either unrecognisable or instantly mesmerising.<br /> <br /> Hideous (0-pt. Flaw)<br /> You are memorably ugly, as a result of some deformity, disfiguring scars, weeping sores, inhuman mutations, or some other curse of the Blood. Your Appearance can never measure how attractive you are; instead, the more dots of Appearance you have, the more intimidatingly horrid you look. You add your Appearance bonus to attempts to threaten, intimidate or unsettle, rather than to charm or persuade.<br /> <br /> You must deduct your Appearance from most seduction attempts.<br /> <br /> Clan Curse: Mark of the Hidden*<br /> All Nosferatu gain the Hideous Flaw. In addition, you must subtract two dice from all social dice pools when interacting with those unused to your horrific visage (this does not stack with the seduction penalty; use the higher of the two). Almost all humans will be repulsed or distracted by the cursed looks of the Clan of the Hidden, though if a target is subject to a Blood Bond to you, this typically reduces the penalty by one for each step they are bound, to a minimum penalty of zero.<br /> <br /> *In my rules, each clan has a Blood Gift (Boon) and a Clan Curse (Bane) to round them out. If you're interested in the former, it's as follows:<br /> <br /> Blood Gift: Tortured Soul<br /> The Embrace is particularly agonising for Nosferatu. When you were turned, your whole body was twisted and warped. But this has made you strong. You gain a +2 dice pool penalty when resisting torture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-21-2021, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T08:10:41-07:00","id":1455439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455294#post1455294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my rules, each clan has a Blood Gift (Boon) and a Clan Curse (Bane) to round them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious what boons do other clans get in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26967-souskind","name":"souskind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T00:49:30-07:00","id":1455488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>souskind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455439#post1455439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious what boons do other clans get in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my rules hack is quite extensive by now, as I use the Exalted 3e base dice pool system (i.e., TN 7, double-10s, 1s don't subtract) with the VTR difficulty system (deduct dice rather than changing TN or successes required), with Exalted 3e's social influence system (i.e., Intimacies, but rated from 1-5 dots). So that has to be borne in mind.<br /> <br /> Quickly:<br /> Assamites - +2 dice to track vampires<br /> Brujah - +2 dice when trying to show intense emotion<br /> Cappadocian (DA): +2 Self-Control/Instinct when in the presence of corpses <br /> Daughters of Cacophony - +2 dice on social influence regarding your favoured emotion<br /> Gangrel - +2 dice on the first round of combat/any fight or flight situation (this also adds to first round movement and Initiative)<br /> Giovanni - As Cappadocian<br /> Harbingers - Can see ghosts in any degree of darkness, with clarity inverse to how dark it is<br /> Lasombra - +2 dice in pitch black (this can be used for anything)<br /> Malkavian - +2 on solving enigmas and finding hidden truths<br /> Nosferatu - +2 versus torture <br /> Ravnos - +2 sleight of hand<br /> Setite - +2 when try to discern weakness<br /> Toreador - +2 when trying to make something beautiful (antis interpret this liberally...)<br /> Tremere - +2 for rituals and ceremonies<br /> Tzimisce - +2 when punishing rulebreakers<br /> Ventrue - +2 when engaging with power structures<br /> <br /> These are not yet balanced and it's worth noting that the Clan Curses are also often tweaked, so that the two together are more balanced. Some of these Blood Gifts are inspired by those from VTR2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-24-2021, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T01:06:52-07:00","id":1455490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455200#post1455200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Obviously, Nosferatu always have to take the Hideous Flaw, and they tend to have high Appearance rather than low, but it means something very different to a Toreador's high Appearance. I like that change to the rules, since Appearance is no longer a dump stat and Nosferatu ugliness is a weapon as much as a Flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who perhaps enjoyed too much getting to put all my social monster Nosferatu's social traits into Manipulation and Charisma, and not having to 'waste' a dot in Appearance to 'look average,' this is perhaps a great idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T01:41:45-07:00","id":1455496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455490#post1455490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who perhaps enjoyed too much getting to put all my social monster Nosferatu's social traits into Manipulation and Charisma, and not having to 'waste' a dot in Appearance to 'look average,' this is perhaps a great idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It works really well. It becomes the default Social stat for many Nosferatu, since you can use it to intimidate others but also to pass unspoken messages to your clanmates in plain sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T06:45:15-07:00","id":1455507,"title":"","content":"Honestly, , If it weren't for the bullshittery around blush of life I feel like feeding through utilizing sexual attraction is probably the wisest feeding strat for those who don't have a lot of control over their environment. Normal looks and great charisma fairs worse than great looks and normal charisma, especially when the music is loud and the people are drunk. This probably goes further in the information age where one browses through faces and can swipe in a particular direction (I wouldn't know about this, I've never seen a woman before). <br /> <br /> You need to invest less xp in making a successful cassanova than you do a sandman (the next best thing) or overlord (the thing after that)<br /> <br /> Appearance 2 is &quot;if I spend the night in the club I might get blood&quot;. Appearance 3 is 'I can go to a club and get blood after some effort&quot;, appearance 4 is &quot;I went to the club and got blood&quot;, appearance 5 is &quot;the blood in the club is mine, it's just waiting for me to walk in&quot;. straight women have it even easier since straight men are the easiest possible target group. The best discipline for the club isn't Presence, it's Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T10:21:27-07:00","id":1455523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455488#post1455488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well my rules hack is quite extensive by now, as I use the Exalted 3e base dice pool system (i.e., TN 7, double-10s, 1s don't subtract) with the VTR difficulty system (deduct dice rather than changing TN or successes required), with Exalted 3e's social influence system (i.e., Intimacies, but rated from 1-5 dots). So that has to be borne in mind.<br /> <br /> Quickly:<br /> Assamites - +2 dice to track vampires<br /> Brujah - +2 dice when trying to show intense emotion<br /> Cappadocian (DA): +2 Self-Control/Instinct when in the presence of corpses<br /> Daughters of Cacophony - +2 dice on social influence regarding your favoured emotion<br /> Gangrel - +2 dice on the first round of combat/any fight or flight situation (this also adds to first round movement and Initiative)<br /> Giovanni - As Cappadocian<br /> Harbingers - Can see ghosts in any degree of darkness, with clarity inverse to how dark it is<br /> Lasombra - +2 dice in pitch black (this can be used for anything)<br /> Malkavian - +2 on solving enigmas and finding hidden truths<br /> Nosferatu - +2 versus torture<br /> Ravnos - +2 sleight of hand<br /> Setite - +2 when try to discern weakness<br /> Toreador - +2 when trying to make something beautiful (antis interpret this liberally...)<br /> Tremere - +2 for rituals and ceremonies<br /> Tzimisce - +2 when punishing rulebreakers<br /> Ventrue - +2 when engaging with power structures<br /> <br /> These are not yet balanced and it's worth noting that the Clan Curses are also often tweaked, so that the two together are more balanced. Some of these Blood Gifts are inspired by those from VTR2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm gonna do some tweaks in my game based on your ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26967-souskind","name":"souskind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T01:55:35-07:00","id":1455561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>souskind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455193-some-simple-ideas-for-appearance-houserules-to-make-it-useful-revised-3e-v20?p=1455523#post1455523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I'm gonna do some tweaks in my game based on your ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might as well check out the full WIP document with Boons/Banes and descriptions, then: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E_GkCZ21_JGrjo9UCTKoXrSplJA0br0bv7m7xv1Vhhk/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t?usp=drivesdk</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}